WHY THIS WORKS
- one short, warm, specific opening question instead of a welcome paragraph
- does not front-load who you are before knowing whether she cares
- matches her length. she wrote four words, so the reply is short

CONVERSATION 1: "SUPPORT"

Lead: SUPPORT

Sonia: Glad you reached out.

What's going on for you at the moment?

Lead: I've been trying for 2 years and nothing is working. I don't know what to do.

Sonia: Two years without answers is a long time to hold on your own.

Has anything been investigated in that time, or has it mostly been waiting?

Lead: I've had bloods and a scan. They said everything looked fine and to keep trying.

Sonia: Fine on those two things covers less ground than it sounds like.

Was your partner's side looked at as well, or only yours?

Lead: Only me. He hasn't been tested at all.

Sonia: Then half the picture is still blank after two years, and that's the first thing I'd fix.

A semen analysis is quick, cheap and it changes what the last two years actually mean. Right now you're both guessing.

Lead: I didn't know that. He's always assumed it's me.

Sonia: Most couples land there by default, not by evidence.

How much of a priority is starting a family for you at the moment, honestly?

Lead: It's the only thing I care about.

Sonia: Then let's take it seriously.

Book a call and my team will go through all of it. Both of you on the call if he'll come. I should say it's a paid coaching program, so that doesn't land as a surprise later.

Lead: That's fine. How do I book?

Sonia: Here.

{{booking_link}}

CONVERSATION 2: "where do I even start?"

Lead: hi, where do I even start? I feel completely lost

Sonia: Start by telling me one thing: how long have you been trying?

Lead: 7 months. I'm 34. Nothing's wrong as far as I know but I feel like I'm behind already.

Sonia: Seven months at 34 with nothing flagged isn't behind. Most healthy couples take up to a year.

Where's the feeling of being lost coming from? The trying itself, or all the information?

Lead: The information. Every account says something different and I've started five different things.

Sonia: Then the problem isn't that you're doing too little. It's that nothing you're doing was chosen for you specifically.

Lead: That's exactly it. I have no idea which of it matters.

Sonia: Nobody would, from the outside. It's not a failure of effort.

Watch my masterclass first. It's free and it'll cut most of what you've collected down to the parts that actually matter.

{{masterclass_link}}

Lead: I'll do that tonight. And if I still want help after?

Sonia: Then message me and we'll talk about whether working together makes sense. No rush at seven months.
